#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Konsep kritikal: {#critical-concepts}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the measurement of a qubit in a superposition is probabilistic, like flipping a coin, the superposition state itself behaves differently than a flipping coin.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun pengukuran qubit dalam superposisi adalah bersifat kebarangkalian, seperti melambung duit syiling, keadaan superposisi itu sendiri berkelakuan berbeza daripada duit syiling yang sedang berputar.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A main difference between a classical probability distribution and a superposition is that the superposition has *phase* coherence, which allows it to interfere constructively or destructively.\n"
msgstr "Perbezaan utama antara taburan kebarangkalian klasik dan superposisi ialah superposisi mempunyai koheren *fasa*, yang membolehkannya berinterferens secara membina atau memusnah.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The state of a single, isolated qubit can be visualized as a point on the so-called \"Bloch sphere,\" where the relative amplitudes of the $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ components determine the polar angle $\\theta$ and the relative phases between the two components determine the azimuthal angle $\\phi$.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan qubit tunggal yang terpencil boleh digambarkan sebagai titik pada apa yang dipanggil \"sfera Bloch,\" di mana amplitud relatif komponen $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$ menentukan sudut kutub $\\theta$ dan fasa relatif antara dua komponen menentukan sudut azimut $\\phi$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "All single-qubit quantum gates can be viewed as rotations of the vector on this sphere.\n"
msgstr "Semua gate kuantum satu qubit boleh dilihat sebagai putaran vektor pada sfera ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F questions: {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Soalan B/S: {#tf-questions}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F A quantum superposition is basically the same as a probabilistic event in classical physics, like flipping a coin.\n"
msgstr "B/S Superposisi kuantum pada dasarnya sama dengan peristiwa kebarangkalian dalam fizik klasik, seperti melambung duit syiling.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The length of the Bloch vector describing the state of a single isolated qubit is always 1.\n"
msgstr "B/S Panjang vektor Bloch yang menggambarkan keadaan qubit tunggal yang terpencil sentiasa 1.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Single-qubit quantum gates do not change the length of the Bloch vector.\n"
msgstr "B/S gate-gate kuantum satu qubit tidak mengubah panjang vektor Bloch.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "MC questions: {#mc-questions}"
msgstr "Soalan pelbagai pilihan: {#mc-questions}"

